Root cause:
The bug occurred because the current page (`mCurPage`) was not set to `null` immediately when the last page was popped, potentially leading to an invalid state where the application might reference a non-existent page during a transition animation. This oversight caused issues with the state management of the page stack, especially when handling transitions, leading to unexpected behavior in the application.
